  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strategic Assistance for Emergency Response in Democratic Republic of Congo (Safer IV)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since November 2019, Mercy Corps, Norwegian Refugee Council (NRC), ACTED, Solidarit&#xE9;s International (SI), and Concern Worldwide have united as one Consortium to deliver Strategic Assistance for Emergency Response (SAFER) in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC); a joint programme to harmonise emergency response among humanitarian actors in DRC, with the overall goal of enabling households affected by conflict and shocks to cover their basic needs. The programme supports the specific outcome of delivering a coordinated humanitarian response that enables vulnerable households affected by conflict and shocks to address their immediate needs with dignity. This includes supporting their safe and equitable access to emergency market based multipurpose cash assistance (MPCA) and basic Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WaSH) services to reduce reliance on negative coping mechanisms to meet the basic needs of conflict and shock affected populations.</narrative>
  </description>
